## 🔍 Code Review Process

**MANDATORY**: All code must undergo review before merging.

### Review Checklist

#### 1. Code Structure Review

- [ ] Legacy and modern code maintain parallel structure
- [ ] Code is organized logically
- [ ] File names are clear and descriptive

#### 2. Modernization Review

- [ ] Modern code demonstrates C# 12–14 features appropriately
- [ ] Before/after comparison is clear
- [ ] Modernization improves code quality (readability, safety, maintainability)

#### 3. Test Review

- [ ] Tests exist for both legacy and modern implementations
- [ ] Same test cases applied to both
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Tests validate correctness and demonstrate benefits

#### 4. Documentation Review

- [ ] **Zero-Copy Policy verified**: Content is transformative, not reformative
- [ ] ADR created for significant decisions
- [ ] Code comments are clear and helpful
- [ ] README updated if structure changed

#### 5. Functional Equivalence Review

- [ ] Legacy and modern implementations behave the same
- [ ] No behavioral changes introduced
- [ ] Modernization is purely language-level

---

## 📝 Review Tools

**Use these tools for code review**:

- `dotnet build` - Build verification
- `dotnet test` - Test execution
- Manual code review - Structure and modernization quality

---

## Review Frequency

- **Before committing**: Review all modified files
- **After modernization**: Review both legacy and modern implementations
- **Periodic audits**: Comprehensive review of modernization examples
- **After major changes**: Full review of affected sections

